There is a huge object identification spoiler on several ways to do so.
Let me give you a few hints without trying to be too spoily.
 o You may notice the game randomizes some characteristics (e.g., the
name, color) of several items at the start of each game. So ELBIB YLOH
is not the same scroll in each game (but will be consistent with a
single game). There are other characteristics that are more consistent
- I will leave deriving those as an exercise to the reader.
 o items that stack will have the same characteristics (e.g., form of
identification, enchantment)
 o items that are more frequent are often "mundane" (e.g., uncursed, no
enchantment); however, there are exceptions
 o some particularly dangerous items are more often generated cursed;
some particularly helpful items are more often generated uncursed or
blessed
 o some monsters have a limited inventory (generally the same items
each time)
 o selling items to store keepers (drop the item & agree to sell it)
may partially identify them - most often with armor or weapons. Note
the store keeper demands far more from you to make purchases than
offers in a sale. The real "price" is usually somewhere in between.
 o some items are identified when you use them or see them in use;
others are not
 o notice that some items are used by monsters (usually against you)
and others are not

